    {
      "id": "lesson-2-7-print-numbers",
      "number": "2.7",
      "title": "Print Numbers",
      "summary": "In Python, you don't need to use quotation marks to print numbers. Unlike strings, numbers can be printed directly.",
      "status": "available",
      "estimatedMinutes": 5,
      "tags": [
        "python-data-types"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-paragraph-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "In Python, you don't need to use quotation marks to print numbers. Unlike strings, numbers can be printed directly.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-heading-2",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "For example, to print the number 5:"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-code-3",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(5)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-code-4",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "5",
          "caption": "Output"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-heading-5",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Click the Run Code button, and you should see 5 printed on the Output screen."
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-paragraph-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "You can also print floating-point numbers (numbers with decimals) the same way:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-code-7",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(343.44)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-code-8",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "343.44",
          "caption": "Output"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-heading-9",
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Click the Run Code button, and you should see 343.44 printed on the Output screen."
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-paragraph-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "No quotes needed — Python understands that you're working with numbers, not text.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-paragraph-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "But what happens if you print numbers with quotation marks?",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-7-paragraph-12",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Let's find out next!",
          "format": "plain"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson-2-8-understanding-numbers-and-strings",
      "number": "2.8",
      "title": "Understanding Numbers and Strings",
      "summary": "Let's print 5 inside quotation marks:",
      "status": "available",
      "estimatedMinutes": 5,
      "tags": [
        "python-data-types"
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Let's print 5 inside quotation marks:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-2",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(\"5\")",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-3",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "5",
          "caption": "Output"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Go ahead — click the Run Code button.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Looks the same as before, right? But here's the catch:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-6",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Even though it looks the same to us, Python sees it differently.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-7",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "- When you write print(5), Python treats it as a number.\n- When you write print(\"5\"), it's a string — just plain text.",
          "format": "markdown"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "And this matters when you try to do math.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Let's see the difference:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "For example:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-11",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(5 + 3)",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-12",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "8",
          "caption": "Output"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-13",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Now try this:",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-14",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "python",
          "code": "print(\"5\" + \"3\")",
          "caption": "Example"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-code-15",
          "type": "code",
          "language": "text",
          "code": "53",
          "caption": "Output"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "When you add numbers without quotation marks, Python performs a mathematical calculation.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-paragraph-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "But when you add numbers with quotes, Python treats them as text and joins them together.",
          "format": "plain"
        },
        {
          "id": "page-2-8-image-18",
          "type": "image",
          "src": "/assets/courses/python-course/python-course-image-04.png",
          "alt": "Idea Emoji",
          "caption": "Idea Emoji",
          "loading": "lazy"
        },
        {
